---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = 'November 7, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — KFit"
  description="KFit privacy policy: local-first health tracking, transparent nutrition sources, encrypted cloud sync in AWS Mumbai, and strict 30-day diagnostic retention."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal-main">
    <div class="container legal-container">
      <div class="legal-header">
        <span class="legal-badge">Legal &amp; Privacy</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-date">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card">
        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>1. Core Philosophy: Local-First Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            KFit is designed from the ground up as a <strong>local-first</strong> wellness companion. Your day-to-day fitness data — meals logged, calorie targets, workout sets, body weight, hydration, and personal notes — is saved locally on your physical device in an encrypted SQLite database.
          </p>
          <p>
            Using core tracking requires <strong>no account signup, no phone number, and no email address</strong>. If you use KFit without signing in, none of your health metrics leave your phone.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2. What Data Leaves Your Phone (When Enabled)</h2>
          <p>Data leaves your device only when you explicitly opt in to connected features:</p>
          
          <h3>A. Optional Cloud Sync &amp; Backups</h3>
          <p>
            If you create an account and sign in (via Google, GitHub, or email):
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your database records synchronize with our cloud database powered by <strong>Supabase</strong>, hosted in <strong>AWS ap-south-1 (Mumbai, India)</strong>.</li>
            <li>Cloud backups are encrypted using AES-256-GCM before transport and storage.</li>
            <li>We retain server snapshots on a strict <strong>30-day rolling retention window</strong>, after which older backups are permanently deleted.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>B. AI Meal Estimates &amp; Food Scanning</h3>
          <p>
            KFit connects to Google Gemini models using your personal Gemini API key to understand meal descriptions and estimate dish portions from photos:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>When you scan a meal or ask the coach, your image or prompt is transmitted directly to Google's API endpoints.</li>
            <li>Your API key is stored securely in your phone's hardware-backed keystore (Android Keystore).</li>
            <li>Depending on your Gemini API tier (free vs. paid), Google's API terms of service govern how prompts are processed. KFit servers never intercept or store your meal photos.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>C. Barcode &amp; Nutrition Lookups</h3>
          <p>
            When searching for packaged foods or scanning barcodes, the app queries public databases including <strong>Open Food Facts</strong> and <strong>USDA FoodData Central</strong>. These lookups transmit only the barcode number or search query string without user identifiers.
          </p>

          <h3>D. Diagnostics &amp; Crash Reports (Opt-In)</h3>
          <p>
            To monitor app stability and fix bugs, KFit can collect diagnostic telemetry:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Diagnostics are collected <strong>only for signed-in users</strong> who have <em>"Share diagnostics"</em> enabled in Settings.</li>
            <li>Reports include error codes, device OS version, app version, and operation latency.</li>
            <li><strong>We never collect or transmit your logged meals, body statistics, journal notes, or photos in telemetry.</strong></li>
            <li>All telemetry events are automatically purged after <strong>30 days</strong>.</li>
            <li>You can disable diagnostics at any time in <em>Settings &rarr; Your data &rarr; Share diagnostics</em>, which immediately deletes any locally queued telemetry.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>3. Compliance with India's DPDP Act</h2>
          <p>
            KFit complies with the Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023 of India:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Lawful Basis &amp; Consent:</strong> We process personal data solely on the basis of your explicit consent and for providing the fitness tracking services you request.</li>
            <li><strong>Purpose Limitation:</strong> Data collected is used strictly for fitness tracking, synchronization, and error resolution. We do not sell data, build advertising profiles, or monetize your personal health information.</li>
            <li><strong>Data Storage Localization:</strong> Cloud synchronization data is hosted in the <strong>AWS ap-south-1 (Mumbai)</strong> region.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>4. Age Restriction &amp; Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            KFit is intended for individuals aged <strong>15 and older</strong>. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 15. If a user is between 15 and 17 years old, the terms require parental or guardian knowledge and consent.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>5. Your Rights: Access, Correction &amp; Deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Under applicable data protection laws, you have the right to:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Access &amp; Export:</strong> Export your full database at any time as an open JSON file directly from <em>Settings &rarr; Backup &rarr; Export</em>.</li>
            <li><strong>Correction:</strong> Update or delete any food entry, weight log, or profile attribute locally in the app.</li>
            <li><strong>Account &amp; Cloud Deletion:</strong> You can request complete erasure of your cloud account, synced tables, and telemetry by emailing <a href="mailto:support@getkfit.app">support@getkfit.app</a> or submitting a request via our <a href="/contact">Contact Form</a>. Deletion requests are processed within 30 days.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>6. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
          <div class="legal-table-wrap">
            <table class="legal-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Provider</th>
                  <th>Purpose</th>
                  <th>Location</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Supabase / AWS</strong></td>
                  <td>User authentication, database sync &amp; backups</td>
                  <td>Mumbai, India (AWS ap-south-1)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Google Gemini</strong></td>
                  <td>Natural language parsing &amp; meal photo scans (via user API key)</td>
                  <td>Google Global Cloud</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Cloudflare</strong></td>
                  <td>Website hosting, contact routing &amp; edge proxy security</td>
                  <td>Global Edge Network</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Open Food Facts</strong></td>
                  <td>Packaged food barcode nutrition lookup</td>
                  <td>France / Global</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>7. Updates to this Policy</h2>
          <p>
            If we make material changes to how we handle user data, we will update this page and present an updated terms acceptance notice within the KFit mobile application.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>8. Contact &amp; Grievance Redressal</h2>
          <p>
            For privacy inquiries, questions regarding this policy, or data erasure requests, please contact our support desk:
          </p>
          <div class="contact-box">
            <p><strong>KFit Support &amp; Privacy Desk</strong></p>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@getkfit.app">support@getkfit.app</a></p>
            <p>Web Form: <a href="/contact">https://getkfit.app/contact</a></p>
            <p>Bangalore, Karnataka, India</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-main {
    padding-top: 100px;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .legal-container {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 20px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .legal-badge {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--apple-blue);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .legal-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-heading);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }

  .legal-date {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .legal-card {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: 48px;
    box-shadow: var(--card-shadow);
  }

  .legal-section {
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  .legal-section:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-heading);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .legal-section h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-heading);
    margin: 18px 0 8px;
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    margin: 8px 0 16px 20px;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--apple-blue);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }

  .legal-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .legal-table th, .legal-table td {
    padding: 12px 14px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .legal-table th {
    color: var(--text-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }

  .contact-box {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .contact-box p {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .legal-card {
      padding: 28px 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
